  "tagline": "Tiny reactive in-memory store for tables and values, with persisters and CRDT sync.",
  "description": "TinyBase is a small TypeScript data store that holds tabular data and key-values in memory, with fine-grained listeners that make React and other UIs update precisely when cells change. Optional modules add indexes, metrics, relationships, a query language (TinyQL) with joins and grouping, undo checkpoints, and persisters to IndexedDB, OPFS, SQLite, PGlite, Postgres, Cloudflare Durable Objects and more. MergeableStore and synchronizers give CRDT-based sync between clients and servers. It suits apps where the working dataset fits in memory and you want reactivity and local-first sync without a heavy framework.",
